ategory="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations> <non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>JP 4132290        U</text> <sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1128117A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO MASAHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBAHARA HIDEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMAKI NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOHO KASEI CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, MASAHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBAHARA, HIDEO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAKI, NOBORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOHO KASEI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO MASAHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBAHARA HIDEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMAKI NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, MASAHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBAHARA, HIDEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAKI, NOBORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A resin pipe joint comprising a flare portion (10a) formed on a pipe (10), an inclined portion (11a) formed internally of a joint body (11), an annular member (12) having inner peripheral surface fitted on the pipe and the outer peripheral surface inserted in the joint body and formed at the end with a tapered chamfered portion (12a), and a pipe clamping member (13) threadedly fitted to the joint body. The pipe clamping member being threadedly fitted to the joint body causes the chamfered portion of the annular member to pressure-contact the flare portion of the pipe and the flare portion of the pipe to pressure-contact the inclined portion in the interior of the joint body, whereby the clamping force can be concentrated on the flare portion of the pipe, so that a high sealing capability between the pipe and the joint body is obtained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un joint pour tuyau en résine. En l'occurrence, un évasement (10a) est réalisé sur un tuyau (10). Un corps de joint (11) présente intérieurement une partie biseautée (11a). Un élément annulaire (12), dont une extrémité est chanfreinée (12a), comporte une surface périphérique intérieure s'appuyant sur le tuyau, et une surface périphérique externe s'insérant dans le corps de joint. En outre, un serre-tube (13) vient se fixer par filetage sur le corps du joint. Le montage fileté du serre-tube fait que la partie chanfreinée de l'élément annulaire exerce une pression de contact sur la partie évasée du tuyau, qui à son tour, exerce sur la partie biseautée une pression de contact à l'intérieur du corps du joint. La force de serrage vient ainsi se concentrer sur la partie évasée du tuyau. Il en résulte une liaison hautement étanche entre le tuyau et le corps du joint.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>